KZ2 patch 4020: the prompt-device switch ignores keys already held when the window comes back to the front.

Hand session 2026-10-22 (session log kz2-20261022-090725.log): pressing F12 (Steam's screenshot key) flipped the
button prompts to keycaps. All six "[pad] last input: keyboard" lines name buttons 0x0800 = R1, whose default keys are
Mouse1 and O; F12 is bound to nothing and pad_kb_eval never sees it. KZ2 4016 takes a key as pressed when it is down
now and was up at the previous poll, and a poll while the window is not in front reads every key as up, so a key that
is held at the first poll back in front (the click that brought the window back, a button the overlay or the desktop
kept down across a focus change) counted as a fresh press: once per focus change, which 4016's own header already
named ("again after a focus change"). Now the edge lives in pad_keybinds.h (pad_kb_edge, host test
tools/runtime/test_pad_kb_edge.sh): the first poll in front takes the held keys as the baseline, and it starts in that
state, so a key held while the game starts does not count either. KZ3 4011's intent is kept: any bound key or mouse
button pressed in the game window switches the prompts to keycaps. The log line names the keys ("(r1:Mouse1)"), and the
window leaving and coming back to the front is logged (first 20) with the keys held at that moment.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

